{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_STEM_Simplified\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by STEM Simplified</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Peter lives near a rectangular field that is filled with blackberry bushes. The field is 10 meters long and 8 meters wide, and Peter can reach any blackberries that are within 1 meter of an edge of the field. The portion of the field he can reach is shaded in the figure below. What fraction of the area of the field can Peter reach?\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2026_amc_8_q6.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/54/2026_amc_8_q6.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"650\" height=\"388\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/056dea0dbd6ab1e19b8b40954988f67ad89d764a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{6}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{1}{4}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{3}{8}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5}\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"408\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can calculate this reachable area to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211be02227c4356872912a9b2115b0ac987aa80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Total area} - \\text{Unreachable area}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"15\" />. The total area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a6442e8f67d1293097e93dad0266f8ed01fa3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 10 = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, and the unreachable area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f835441c98de9178034206e214456f8fc0d18aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8-2)(10-2) = 6\\cdot 8 = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a8818449d73c664072079038d52a594a41745dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{80-48}{80} = \\frac{32}{80} = \\boxed{ \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"193\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~OlympiadMaster\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each \"region\" is one unit from an edge. Thus, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the length and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the width of the unshaded region. Then, it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/8038b0cb8dfb6b40bb07ce4d1d702c90c16bc8fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = 10 - 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c653ab833453fc2794b7b9b5efb42d76372822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = 8 - 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />, and the unshaded regions dimensions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22502aeb762125f5f1d8786beadbcd287716de69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Then, the area of the shaded region is the area of the total region subtracted by the area of the unshaded region, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c2ed50be5eacab8fea321cebaa3057f378662e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80 - 48 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71ff0b99949983dd632b85022912a9597acf2bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{un}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />. Then, the ratio is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f6b21580d6f49517a1df00030e0181b03bb626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32/80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/7/ad7b306f5b4cbd97a28a28604234005b96a17805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"26\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By rearranging the diagram, the unreachable (white) region can be moved to the lower-left corner without changing the shaded area. The reachable region then forms an L-shaped figure composed of two rectangles.\n</p><p>One rectangle has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561ba7888389f23b876fc338780023856275a6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8\\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and the other has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f181c49d3d5f3894d0d0c56bf410414e3f18439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. These rectangles overlap in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/7901356dd65ec4da1b694937cc4ffc663e90d800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times 2$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> square, which must be subtracted once.\n</p><p>Thus, the area of the shaded region is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa947b68d10eb546aac3309038f1ca85179c62b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8\\cdot 2)+(10\\cdot 2)-(2\\cdot 2)=2(10+8-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The total area of the field is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a663db1d67ded68621431f423a121a3fef8a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot 8=80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Dividing, the fraction of the field Peter can reach is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d23ddd704409aa1e2a5e86ba9f2a790457ade1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2(10+8-2)}{80}=\\dfrac{10+8-2}{40}=\\dfrac{16}{40}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{2}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"347\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~jeremyq\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can first start off by finding the unreachable area. The problem tells us that the distance between the reachable and unreachable area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get the dimensions of the unreachable to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d860571117a97a3da4635dc8d5411f0aaab9c134.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02f33a1cdab33456368c9e12abe97f4aca7fd48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 = 10 - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4d575206903e4057e16955672bf5a236139b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 = 8 - 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, the area of the unreachable is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, the problem asks us to find the fraction of area he can reach, so we need to get area of the entire field and subtract by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.Since the entire field is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a6442e8f67d1293097e93dad0266f8ed01fa3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 10 = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />,  we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/c/48c2ed50be5eacab8fea321cebaa3057f378662e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80 - 48 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. So the area of the part Peter can reach is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, to convert this to a fraction of the entire field, we can do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60dd087f5d4030b545bb9d95bb986f0c8cad3ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{32}{80}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a08aff9228cf7347bc9b7273a77a1a57fe5d0746.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{32}{80} = \\boxed{ \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{2}{5} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"106\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~Ingeniouspeacock36\n</p><p>To add on, its just like calculating the total area- the unwanted recangular area.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U\">https://youtu.be/gzXlOkLl24U</a>\n</p><p>~TheSmartGreekMathDude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk\">https://youtu.be/nY1hhVbEeBk</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_STEM_Simplified\">Video Solution by STEM Simplified</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by STEM Simplified\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIdnkWC7_Cg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MIdnkWC7_Cg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FLhek5RXugY\">https://youtu.be/FLhek5RXugY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=513s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3GmtxMC-W1I&amp;t=513s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV13LMe6zESm/\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV13LMe6zESm/</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8\" title=\"2026 AMC 8\">2026 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Prece